  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "The Eiffel Tower leans away from the sun, and nobody is pushing it.",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.52
    },
    {
      "text": "Imagine visiting Paris on a blazing summer afternoon.",
      "start": 3.76,
      "end": 6.02
    },
    {
      "text": "You take a picture of the tower. It looks completely still, but that enormous iron structure is quietly changing shape.",
      "start": 6.42,
      "end": 11.86
    },
    {
      "text": "First, the metal warms up, then the tower grows a little taller, and here comes the strange part.",
      "start": 12.26,
      "end": 16.72
    },
    {
      "text": "The side facing the sun heats up more than the side in the shade, so one side stretches more than the other.",
      "start": 17.1,
      "end": 21.94
    },
    {
      "text": "The result? The top bends away from the sunlight.",
      "start": 22.22,
      "end": 24.28
    },
    {
      "text": "The tower is basically trying to find some shade, very slowly and very unsuccessfully.",
      "start": 24.64,
      "end": 28.68
    },
    {
      "text": "You see, iron isn't perfectly still inside. Its atoms vibrate, heat them up, and their average spacing increases.",
      "start": 28.68,
      "end": 34.34
    },
    {
      "text": "Tiny changes add up across an entire tower. Think of two friends walking arm in arm.",
      "start": 34.84,
      "end": 39.08
    },
    {
      "text": "If one takes slightly longer steps, the pair starts turning.",
      "start": 39.42,
      "end": 42.06
    },
    {
      "text": "Uneven expansion gives the tower a similar little bend.",
      "start": 42.44,
      "end": 44.7
    },
    {
      "text": "As the sun moves across the sky, the summit can trace a curve roughly 15 centimeters across.",
      "start": 45.1,
      "end": 49.42
    },
    {
      "text": "Too small for you to notice. Completely normal for the tower.",
      "start": 49.96,
      "end": 52.6
    },
    {
      "text": "When the iron cools, it contracts again, so that famous Paris landmark spends its sunny days",
      "start": 52.94,
      "end": 57.58
    },
    {
      "text": "doing the world's slowest sun dodge.",
      "start": 57.58,
      "end": 59.38
    }
  ],
